# cw119, the crooked map (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 2: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle cw119
revision 2
state ready
dialect coldwater
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for cty_heather_fernwood
written_by claude-codex-cw-1
title the crooked map
fits stage=adult|old
prefers talk=quiet warmth=warm
traits temper=even talk=quiet warmth=warm humour=none honesty=guarded piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk quotes_old_sayings_for_everything
likes smoked_eel digging old_maps thunder
dislikes early_bells night_noise
fears a_harvest_lost_to_rot a_family_trade_forgotten
hopes a_tree_that_keeps_bearing a_garden_with_room_to_grow
topics work +0.5 memories +0.4 home +0.4 food +0.3 travel +0.3 gossip -0.4
styles comfort=practical gossip=reluctant refuse=soft tease=dry
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# sorts #apples# with an old #saying# on the tongue, keeps a crooked #map# folded in a #pocket#, and digs until the #soil# loosens.

words
oath! = Branch and basket | Thunder over the orchard
saying! = A sound apple does not fear the knife | A road drawn straight can still lead astray
apple = apple | orchard apple
apples = apples | picked fruit
basket = basket | picking basket
branch = branch | fruit branch
tree = tree | apple tree
trees = trees | orchard trees
orchard = orchard | apple grove
ladder = ladder | picking ladder
crate = crate | wooden crate
crates = crates | wooden crates
fruit = fruit | gathered crop
bruise = bruise | soft spot
rot = rot | brown spoilage
drying = drying | fruit drying
rack = rack | drying rack
racks = racks | drying racks
knife = knife | trimming blade
skin = skin | apple skin
garden = garden | kitchen garden
spade = spade | digging spade
soil = soil | dark earth
seed = seed | seed grain
root = root | plant root
map = map | old road map
fold = fold | paper crease
ink = ink | faded ink
road = road | high road
path = path | narrow way
step = step | footfall
window = window | house window
door = door | house door
lake = lake | Glasswater
pocket = pocket | coat pocket
eel = eel | smoked eel
smoke = smoke | curing smoke
plate = plate | supper plate
roof = roof | sound roof
thunder = thunder | storm's rumble
bell = bell | early bell
noise = noise | late clatter
night = night | dark hours
morning = morning | first light
coin = coin | pay
price = price | asking cost
@2 saying = saying | old proverb

any
opinion @1 dole for 1 : A hungry neighbour needs a #plate#, not a lecture. | A good #basket# has room for the fruit too bruised to sell.
opinion @1 merchants against 2 : I sort every #apple# and still hear the #price# set as if nobody worked. | The seller counts #coin# while I count what the #tree# bore.
opinion @1 houses against 1 : The #orchard# lasts longer than any crest nailed above it. | Let a House carry the #basket# for a day before calling the crop easy.
opinion @1 city against 1 : The city would drown out the #trees# with #noise#. | I would lose my way there even with a #map# in hand.
opinion @1 newcomers mixed 1 : A new picker can learn which #branch# bends before the #ladder# goes up. | I will give a stranger the sound #crate# if they do their share.
opinion @1 strangers mixed 1 : Someone can share a #plate# without learning all my worries. | I tell a traveller which #road# bends, then let them choose.
opinion @1 road mixed 0 : The old #map# lies about turns, but it remembers where someone once hoped to go. | I trust a walked #path# over a line of #ink#.
opinion @1 festivals mixed 0 : A festival is tolerable under a #roof# when the singing stays gentle. | I would rather walk the #orchard# at its quiet end.

grown
line @1 greet : #greet#. A sound #apple# for you if you want it. | #greet#. The #basket# can wait while we speak.
line @2 greet [pair.band=strangers] : #greet#. Which #road# led you here? | #greet#. Give me a plain word before asking for mine.
line @3 greet [pair.band=friends|family] : I kept the best #apple# from the last #basket#. | Come see where the #garden# took root.
line @4 greet [self.working=yes] : #greet#. I must clear this #rack# first. | I can hear you while I sort the #crates#.
line @5 greet [here.time=dawn] : #greet#. That #bell# found me too soon. | #greet#. The #trees# are quiet before the carts.
line @1 greet.return : Back again? I have a new #saying# if you can bear it. | #welcome_back#. The #basket# is lighter now.
line @2 greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : I have a #plate# set aside. | Did the #map# get you where you meant to go?
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : Come in. The #plate# is by the fire. | The last #apple# is yours if you want it.
line @1 again.open : We have spoken twice before this #crate# filled. | The same #road# brought you back quickly.
line @1 farewell : #saying.capitalize#. Walk carefully. | #farewell#. Mind the #root# beside the #path#.
line @1 farewell.return : Bring back a better #map# if you find one. | I will save an #apple# next time.
line @1 react.news : I will hear it; the #rack# can wait. | Tell me what your own eyes witnessed.
line @1 react.news.new : No word of that reached the #orchard#. | Who came by the #road# with this news?
line @1 react.news.known : A little of that came with the last #crate#. | The first part reached me; what happened afterward?
line @1 react.news.doubt : A #map# can be drawn in error; I want a second account. | That story needs a clearer #path# through its facts.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : I am sorry. Sit under the #roof# a while. | That is bitter fruit to carry home.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : That is a sound #apple# of news. | Good. May they have a peaceful night for that happiness.
line @1 answer.how : The #garden# needs me, but I am well. | Tired. The #apples# are nearly sorted.
line @1 answer.how.busy [self.working=yes] : One #crate# after another today. | Busy with #fruit# and the #drying# #racks#.
line @1 ask.how : Have you found a quiet #path# today? | Did you get a full #plate# at supper?
line @1 sympathise : I can bring you a #plate# and listen. | Take the time you need to speak.
line @1 reassure : A bent #branch# can still bear an #apple#. | Let the #soil# rest tonight; try the #spade# tomorrow.
line @1 decline : I cannot leave the #fruit# on the #rack#. | A false promise would cost you more than my refusal.
line @1 accept_decline : Fair enough; the #map# stays folded. | I hear you. That matter can rest now.
line @1 thank : You carried the #crate# when I could not. Thank you. | I know what that kindness cost you.
line @1 deflect_thanks : I had a spare #apple#. | The #basket# was going your way.
line @1 preclose : I must finish the #drying# before night. | The #garden# needs one last look.
line @1 tease [pair.band=friends] : Your #map# would send us through the #lake#. | That #spade# has done more leaning than digging.
line @1 ack : #bc_right#. I will mark the #crate#. | #bc_fair_enough#. The #path# is clear.
line @1 give.advice : Check the #branch# before leaning the #ladder#. | Turn the #soil# while it is damp, not wet.
line @1 warn [world.bandits=near] : Keep to the #road# with other carts. | Do not follow a strange #path# after dusk.
scene first_picking
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I feel an #apple# for softness before I put it in the #basket#. | A #bruise# under the #skin# will show itself by tomorrow.
b : Can you tell by touch? | Do you throw it away?
a : Usually. My paws have had practice. | No. It may still be good for supper.

scene ladder_foot
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I set the #ladder# where the #soil# is firm. | A high #branch# is not worth a fall into the #crates#.
b : Do you climb far? | Does anyone hold it?
a : Only as far as I can reach safely. | When the ground is uneven.

scene fruit_on_rack
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I lay the cut #fruit# apart on the #rack#. | Damp pieces turn to #rot# if I crowd them.
b : How long do they dry? | Do you turn them?
a : Until they bend without wetness. | When one side has had the air.

scene old_hands
when topic=memories
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I learned the #orchard# work from hands older than mine. | A #saying# comes out of my mouth when I hear the #ladder# creak.
b : Do you remember who taught you? | Does the saying help?
a : Every one of them. | It makes me check my footing.

scene three_harvests
when topic=family
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : My family kept this #orchard# trade before I could lift a #basket#. | I hear an old warning whenever I reach for a high #branch#.
b : Do you feel watched? | Would you leave the work?
a : By memory, perhaps. | I might, but I would still know an #apple# by touch.

scene digging_hour
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Once the #crates# are done, I dig in the #garden#. | Digging asks for no talk, only a firm #step#.
b : What do you plant? | Does it rest you?
a : Whatever #seed# the season will take. | More than sitting indoors.

scene roots_in_soil
when topic=home
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I loosen #soil# around the #root# without pulling at it. | A #garden# can fail if I hurry the smallest task.
b : Does the plant recover? | Do you garden alone?
a : Usually, if the #root# stays whole. | I like the quiet of it.

scene map_crease
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : My old #map# has a #fold# across a road that moved years ago. | I keep it for the marks someone put in the margins.
b : Is it still useful? | Can you read the old writing?
a : For remembering, yes. | Some. The #ink# has faded.

scene wrong_turn
when topic=travel
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : The #map# shows a #path# where the reeds have taken it back. | A traveller who trusts old #ink# may need dry boots afterward.
b : Did you follow it? | Which way do you go now?
a : Once. I turned back at the wet ground. | I ask someone who has walked it lately.

scene smoked_eel
when topic=food
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A little smoked #eel# makes a plain #plate# worth sitting for. | I like the #smoke# on the #skin# when the flesh is still soft.
b : Do you cook it again? | Do you share it?
a : Just warm it beside the fire. | If there is more than one bite.

scene thunder_roof
when topic=weather here.weather=storm
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I like #thunder# from under a sound #roof#. | A storm makes the #trees# move like they are speaking together.
b : Will you inspect them when it quiets? | Does it frighten you?
a : When the wind eases. | No. I watch the #roof# for loose thatch.

scene early_bell
when topic=day here.time=dawn
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : That #bell# speaks before I have thought of breakfast. | I can hear the #bell# through the orchard's quiet.
b : Do you need it to wake? | Would you silence it?
a : The work would wake me soon enough. | For one morning, gladly.

scene night_noise
when topic=day here.time=night
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A loud #noise# at night makes the next #morning# heavy. | I leave the #window# closed when the street will not settle.
b : Does sleep come at all? | Do you complain?
a : Eventually. I am less kind at dawn. | Only when it keeps the whole house awake.

scene sorted_crates
when topic=prices
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A sound #crate# should bring a fair #price#. | The #fruit# I put aside still cost a day of work.
b : Does the buyer see that? | Can you sell the bruised ones?
a : Some do. I remember those buyers. | For less, if they are fit to eat.

scene basket_shared
when topic=friends
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I will carry another #basket# if a neighbour's paws are tired. | A #crate# can be shared without making a speech of it.
b : Do they help you later? | Do you ask first?
a : Some do. That is not why I offer. | I look for the heavy load.

scene quiet_festival
when topic=festival
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I watch a festival from the end of the #road#. | The songs sound better once the shouting has thinned.
b : Do you join in? | Why stay at the edge?
a : For a little while. | I can leave before the #noise# begins.

scene autumn_rack
when topic=season here.season=autumn
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Autumn fills the #rack# faster than I can clear it. | I save the firmest #apples# for the last #crate#.
b : Are those for winter? | Do you work late?
a : Some, if they keep sound. | Until the cut #fruit# is safe from damp.

story crooked_road [topic=travel self.age>=25]
  : I followed the #map# to a turn that no longer existed.
  : The #path# ended in wet ground, so I folded the paper and found a higher way.
  b : Otherwise someone else would follow it. Did you mark the change?
  : I put a new line in the margin. The old one is still there to remind me.

story grandmother_saying [topic=memories self.age>=25]
  : I heard an elder say a sound #apple# would not fear the #knife#.
  : I thought it meant to cut every fruit, until they showed me how to feel for a #bruise#.
  b : It sounds useful beyond the orchard. Do you still say it?
  : Too often, according to some at #home#.

story wet_rack [topic=work self.age>=25]
  : I found rain blowing through a gap above the #rack#.
  : I moved the #fruit# under the #roof# before searching for a board to cover it.
  ask : Did any of it spoil?
  b : The top layer would have caught the rain.
  : A little. The rest dried once the air cleared.

rule @bark_saying
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 8h
say #saying.capitalize#. | There is an old #saying# for this, somewhere.

rule @bark_crate
when concept=bark self.working=yes
does aside
cooldown 7h
say That #crate# wants another look. | The #rack# needs room for the next #basket#.

rule @bark_thunder
when concept=bark here.weather=storm
does aside
cooldown 10h
say Good #thunder#, from under this #roof#. | I hope the #ladder# is put away.

rule @bark_map
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 11h
say This #map# has one turn wrong. | A new #fold# may hide the old #path#.

dlg @1 resident.hub : #greet#. I have a sound #apple# if you want it. | #greet#. Mind the #crates# by the #door#.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : Back again? Was that #map# of any use? | I know you now. What brings you through the #orchard#?
dlg @1 resident.job : I pick #apples#, sort the #fruit#, and tend the #drying# #racks#. | The #basket# is mine until the last #crate# is marked.
dlg @1 resident.bye : #farewell#. Watch the #root# near the #path#. | #saying.capitalize#. Walk carefully.
graft resident.hub
choice Why keep a map with wrong roads? -> map
node map
say Its old #ink# shows where people once travelled. I have marked the turns that changed.
free
choice Do you use it to travel? -> routes
choice Back to what we were saying. -> hub
node routes
say I take it along, then ask someone who has walked the #road# this season.
choice Back to what we were saying. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye
